The 'board setup constraints courtyard' block had:
    DRC_CONSTRAINT courtyardClearanceConstraint( COURTYARD_CLEARANCE_CONSTRAINT );
    holeToHoleConstraint.Value().SetMin( 0 );  // <-- wrong local!
    rule->AddConstraint( courtyardClearanceConstraint );

The middle line wrote to a stack-local from a rule dozens of lines
earlier (already copied into a different rule) — no-op on the state
actually being added. courtyardClearanceConstraint was added with its
default value.

The default happens to also be 0 today so behaviour is unchanged, but
the intent was to be explicit — a future default change would silently
break this. Change it to write on the correct local
(courtyardClearanceConstraint) so the intent is preserved.
---
 pcbnew/drc/drc_engine.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pcbnew/drc/drc_engine.cpp b/pcbnew/drc/drc_engine.cpp
index 7357049c..c0251fae 100644
--- a/pcbnew/drc/drc_engine.cpp
+++ b/pcbnew/drc/drc_engine.cpp
@@ -230,7 +230,15 @@ void DRC_ENGINE::loadImplicitRules()
 
     rule = createImplicitRule( _( "board setup constraints courtyard" ), DRC_IMPLICIT_SOURCE::BOARD_SETUP_CONSTRAINT );
     DRC_CONSTRAINT courtyardClearanceConstraint( COURTYARD_CLEARANCE_CONSTRAINT );
-    holeToHoleConstraint.Value().SetMin( 0 );
+    // Typo fix: this used to be `holeToHoleConstraint.Value().SetMin( 0 );`
+    // which was a copy-paste from the earlier holeToHole block. It wrote to
+    // the local `holeToHoleConstraint` (already copied into a different
+    // rule dozens of lines above), so it was a no-op that left the newly
+    // created `courtyardClearanceConstraint` at its default-constructed
+    // value. The default constraint value happens to also be 0 today, so
+    // behaviour is unchanged — but the intent needs to be explicit here
+    // so a future default change doesn't silently mis-init courtyard.
+    courtyardClearanceConstraint.Value().SetMin( 0 );
     rule->AddConstraint( courtyardClearanceConstraint );
 
     // 2a) micro-via specific defaults (new DRC doesn't treat microvias in any special way)
